{"title":"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TechMath_Thinker\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TechMath Thinker</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Telescoping)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Telescoping)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Hockey_Stick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Hockey Stick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Combinatorial_Method)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Combinatorial Method)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(elegant)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (elegant)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the remainder when<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d24022c5c24f244417fc52eecd6c4daacd8d356.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{\\binom{3}{2}}{2} + \\binom{\\binom{4}{2}}{2} + \\dots +  \\binom{\\binom{40}{2}}{2}\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"53\" />is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/pGkLAX381_s?t=1035\">https://youtu.be/pGkLAX381_s?t=1035</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4O1xiUYjnwE\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4O1xiUYjnwE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TechMath_Thinker\">Video Solution by TechMath Thinker</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TechMath Thinker\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/pVC7nhO79Bg\">https://youtu.be/pVC7nhO79Bg</a>\n</p><p>~ midnight_rain\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Telescoping.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Telescoping)\">Solution 1 (Telescoping)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Telescoping)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first write the expression as a summation.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a48f83d45954f9a10edffa19f815718b3fa0d34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\binom{\\binom{i}{2}}{2}  &amp; = \\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\binom{\\frac{i \\left( i - 1 \\right)}{2}}{2} \\\\ &amp; = \\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\frac{\\frac{i \\left( i - 1 \\right)}{2} \\left( \\frac{i \\left( i - 1 \\right)}{2}- 1 \\right)}{2} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{8} \\sum_{i=3}^{40}  i \\left( i - 1 \\right) \\left( i \\left( i - 1 \\right) - 2 \\right)  \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{8} \\sum_{i=3}^{40} i(i - 1)(i^2-i-2) \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{8} \\sum_{i=3}^{40} i(i-1)(i+1)(i-2) \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{8}\\sum_{i=3}^{40} (i-2)(i-1)i(i+1) \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{40}\\sum_{i=3}^{40}[(i-2)(i-1)i(i+1)(i+2)-(i-3)(i-2)(i-1)i(i+1)]* \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{38\\cdot39\\cdot40\\cdot41\\cdot42-0}{40}\\\\ &amp; = 38 \\cdot 39 \\cdot 41 \\cdot 42 \\\\ &amp; = \\left( 40 - 2 \\right) \\left( 40 - 1 \\right) \\left( 40 + 1 \\right) \\left( 40 + 2 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\left( 40^2 - 2^2 \\right) \\left( 40^2 - 1^2 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\left( 40^2 - 4 \\right) \\left( 40^2 - 1 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = 40^4 - 40^2 \\cdot 5 + 4 \\\\ &amp; \\equiv \\boxed{004}\\pmod{1000}\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"620\" height=\"631\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/289b4f9acf66378f3108d582ee2cfe6a4a96e750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$*(i-2)(i-1)i(i+1)=\\frac{1}{5}[(i-2)(i-1)i(i+1)(i+2)-(i-3)(i-2)(i-1)i(i+1)]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"668\" height=\"38\" /> is how we force the expression to telescope.\n~qyang\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Hockey_Stick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Hockey_Stick)\">Solution 2 (Hockey Stick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Hockey Stick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Doing simple algebra calculation will give the following equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d55d8589ef5f1ce6c86169f06e0221716033106.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\binom{\\binom{n}{2}}{2} &amp;= \\frac{\\frac{n(n-1)}{2} \\cdot (\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}-1)}{2}\\\\  &amp;= \\frac{n(n-1)(n^2-n-2)}{8}\\\\  &amp;= \\frac{(n+1)n(n-1)(n-2)}{8}\\\\  &amp;= \\frac{(n+1)!}{8\\cdot (n-3)!} = 3 \\cdot \\frac{(n+1)!}{4!\\cdot (n-3)!}\\\\  &amp;= 3 \\binom{n+1}{4} \\end{align*}\" width=\"298\" height=\"254\" />\n</p><p>Next, by using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hockey-Stick_Identity\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Hockey-Stick Identity\">Hockey-Stick Identity</a>, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbb1995b74d67a8d6bb206add9258c19a8226cf1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 \\cdot \\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\binom{i+1}{4} = 3 \\binom{42}{5} = 42 \\cdot 41 \\cdot 39 \\cdot 38\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/3/2c3c1e71d29638ced24b536396697a647d8777e4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=(40^2-2^2)(40^2-1^2) \\equiv \\boxed{004} ~(\\text{mod}~ 1000)\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seems like a completely arbitrary number, we can use Engineer's Induction by listing out the first few sums. These are, in the order of how many terms there are starting from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> term: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/8/848ec5b5f695afbacb864efead154761481780c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c7116bbc884d2cf49e25754864ae00d9c42d2d90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/6/71631bb161800df77838e083a7cd360e7024ecfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$378$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8a61e60b64da8bc02c479fe2682ebc9726c7482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$756$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Notice that these are just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/911f76e54381432f055a142fea6e6fdb14567d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\dbinom50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"61\" height=\"55\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/760b3c1c73ba7eea2bf9e128494a9b39a8e1f67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\dbinom61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"61\" height=\"55\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcb9c993c18f78343c63d3f37c26d4a253fbab92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\dbinom72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"61\" height=\"55\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84fc3262ca983b267facda512254cd19f67393da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\dbinom83$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"61\" height=\"55\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c18e2d3734f20f2584ea97cf8b83db8fa0420e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\dbinom94$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"61\" height=\"55\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b826ef3ef3352bc6d49ad472bebf7272260fc212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\dbinom{10}5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"70\" height=\"55\" />. It's clear that this pattern continues up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5e2e4c4950cff11894abd202aa2949e21819c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> terms, noticing that the \"indexing\" starts with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d48495941631dc6e082838d52159da61fcadbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> instead of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b225202c638f073fe7c93a166d35e2ff7f4ffd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" />. Thus, the value of the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82adcef50c073ab20ec4387fe42139b9d207418d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot \\dbinom{42}{37}=2552004 \\equiv \\boxed{\\textbf{004}} \\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"322\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>~A1001\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in solution 1, obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/743341848178cf137090da65755dc52ea0a55c45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\binom{\\binom{i}{2}}{2} = \\frac{1}{8} \\sum_{i=3}^{40} i^4-2i^3-i^2+2i.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"288\" height=\"55\" /> Write this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9e3f2b9e6f3ddad6818667ee6c0997c90f4782f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\sum_{i=3}^{40} i^4 - 2\\sum_{i=3}^{40}i^3 - \\sum_{i=3}^{40}i^2 + 2\\sum_{i=3}^{40}i\\right).\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>We can safely write this expression as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f82d253a613d60779b8078d04d22edd3c56f7c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{40} i^4 - 2\\sum_{i=1}^{40}i^3 - \\sum_{i=1}^{40}i^2 + 2\\sum_{i=1}^{40}i\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"299\" height=\"55\" />, since plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ed4b89a6aeb4814026a2be01bde8bd7d264b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f3e5193f4abdbaf8c424028753f296dac345eb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=2$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/a/37aec1f23058f08ad27ae7b04c0a94734fd608ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^4-2i^3-i^2+2i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" /> both equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/ced6b9b2e75857b566f1e516560c4a4d63977299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> meaning they won't contribute to the sum.\n</p><p>Use the sum of powers formulae. We obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a364d3245dbc76fcec49009f3e292e58844b8403.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\frac{i(i+1)(2i+1)(3i^2+3i-1)}{30} - \\frac{i^2(i+1)^2}{2} - \\frac{i(i+1)(2i+1)}{6} + i(i+1)\\right) \\text{ where i = 40.}\\]\" width=\"699\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>We can factor the following expression as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/edadccff5b6688adfe30ce94daf31184a652f457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\frac{i(i+1)(2i+1)(3i^2+3i-6)}{30} - \\frac{i(i+1)}{2} (i(i+1)-2)\\right),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"468\" height=\"45\" /> and simplifying, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/2058f0f22894a0ba1d8fec8cc97456bafda41f70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\binom{\\binom{i}{2}}{2} = \\frac{i(i+1)(2i+1)(i^2+i-2)}{80}-\\frac{i^2(i+1)^2-2i(i+1)}{16} \\text{ where i = 40.}\\]\" width=\"597\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bd98674413c1b1fad52b875404ca43c9b5d0157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> and simplifying gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/7790c2481a9bc57288fc8ee2186cecdf2b9512c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41\\cdot 81\\cdot 819 - 5\\cdot 41\\cdot 819,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"17\" /> so we would like to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/6/4667789420d69afb9dc889f25f2d7cd7bb3d0c5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$819\\cdot 76\\cdot 41 \\pmod{1000}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" /> To do this, get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed6f36151bbe62019f5942abe13c79749cdfcdc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$819\\cdot 76\\equiv 244 \\pmod{1000}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"216\" height=\"20\" /> Next, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/ade95058033c7fb1e329b5324e67cce483d73b82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$244\\cdot 41 \\equiv \\boxed{004} \\pmod{1000}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"228\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>-sirswagger21\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To solve this problem, we need to use the following result:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/892527bd79ffaa0fb43c423064a350b1641b25b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\sum_{i=n}^m \\binom{i}{k} = \\binom{m+1}{k+1} - \\binom{n}{k+1} . \\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Now, we use this result to solve this problem.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/4/3f45b47ff17a5db5f3a61352027ae93726fb1195.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\binom{\\binom{i}{2}}{2}  &amp; = \\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\binom{\\frac{i \\left( i - 1 \\right)}{2}}{2} \\\\ &amp; = \\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\frac{\\frac{i \\left( i - 1 \\right)}{2} \\left( \\frac{i \\left( i - 1 \\right)}{2}- 1 \\right)}{2} \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{8} \\sum_{i=3}^{40}  i \\left( i - 1 \\right) \\left( i \\left( i - 1 \\right) - 2 \\right)  \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{1}{8} \\sum_{i=3}^{40}  i \\left( i - 1 \\right)  \\left( \\left( i - 2 \\right) \\left( i - 3 \\right) + 4 \\left( i - 2 \\right) \\right)  \\\\ &amp; = 3 \\left( \\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\binom{i}{4} + \\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\binom{i}{3} \\right) \\\\ &amp; = 3 \\left( \\binom{41}{5} - \\binom{3}{5} + \\binom{41}{4} - \\binom{3}{4} \\right) \\\\ &amp; = 3 \\left( \\binom{41}{5} + \\binom{41}{4} \\right) \\\\ &amp; = 3 \\cdot \\frac{41 \\cdot 40 \\cdot 39 \\cdot 38}{5!} \\left( 37 + 5 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = 3 \\cdot 41 \\cdot 13 \\cdot 38 \\cdot 42 \\\\ &amp; = 38 \\cdot 39 \\cdot 41 \\cdot 42 \\\\ &amp; = \\left( 40 - 2 \\right) \\left( 40 - 1 \\right) \\left( 40 + 1 \\right) \\left( 40 + 2 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\left( 40^2 - 2^2 \\right) \\left( 40^2 - 1^2 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = \\left( 40^2 - 4 \\right) \\left( 40^2 - 1 \\right) \\\\ &amp; = 40^4 - 40^2 \\cdot 5 + 4  . \\end{align*}\" width=\"417\" height=\"621\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, modulo 1000, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076df463ff93a285448f5cb6cc224684b3235b40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=3}^{40} \\binom{\\binom{i}{2}}{2}  \\equiv \\boxed{\\textbf{(004) }}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"167\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Combinatorial_Method.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Combinatorial_Method)\">Solution 6 (Combinatorial Method)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Combinatorial Method)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We examine the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/465294d423f343eec4510faaa0ba5e0398280b63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{\\binom{n}{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"54\" height=\"55\" />. Imagine we have a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers. Then the expression can be translated to the number of pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> element subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>To count this, note that each pair of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> element subsets can either share <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> value or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values. In the former case, pick three integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d41d6d69007b91562901dd96aff7823b71639a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{n}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"35\" height=\"53\" /> ways to select these integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to pick which one of the three is the shared integer. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d87d702bf2ee1882dba921fdd1e59c735bc291c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot \\binom{n}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"63\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>In the latter case, we pick <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a4b7a2c254c14f63e977ff0fb015d1c38dad341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{n}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"41\" height=\"55\" /> ways. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d49592c3cc83f1d6618d2e7632f6d1b9a1322d69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\binom{4}{2} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"85\" height=\"55\" /> ways to split this up into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> integers — <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/54216aeffa0fa278199cd3ceeb64cc8400c4a8cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{4}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"39\" height=\"55\" /> ways to pick which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> integers are together and dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to prevent overcounting. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3f56c4da763a5c8bf225874a6df69acea573be0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot \\binom{n}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"63\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>So we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da2ed95355c55ca9f31a196246ab9c950a2bf26.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{\\binom{n}{2}}{2} = 3\\cdot \\binom{n}{3} + 3\\cdot \\binom{n}{4}\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"53\" />\nWe use the Hockey Stick Identity to evaluate this sum:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/9/4791a65035973324ca5d3412a81e58da4ff91989.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{n=3}^{40} \\binom{\\binom{n}{2}}{2} &amp;= \\sum_{n=3}^{40} \\left( 3 \\binom{n}{3} + 3 \\binom{n}{4} \\right) \\\\ &amp;= 3 \\left( \\sum_{n=3}^{40}  \\binom{n}{3} \\right) + 3\\left( \\sum_{n=4}^{40}  \\binom{n}{4} \\right) \\\\ &amp;= 3\\left( \\binom{41}{4} + \\binom{41}{5} \\right) \\end{align*}\" width=\"339\" height=\"174\" />\nEvaluating while accounting for mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> gives the final answer to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4f4f09947c92327e7d182958ea35576dd11af8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{004}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~ GoatPotato\n</p><p><br />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/9/2b9965ff07676aacb6e0282e124ebd21b7734c9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{n}{3}+\\binom{n}{4}=\\binom{n+1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"197\" height=\"55\" /> (Pascal's identity), so this result is consistent with other solutions. ~TThB0501\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28elegant.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(elegant)\">Solution 6 (elegant)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (elegant)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>think about an n-gon. nc2= amount of ways to make an edge. (nc2)c2=amount of ways to pick two random edges out of these edges. however, we can reconstruct this. since no edge will be picked twice, there will either be 3 points or 4 points used in the edges. if there are 3 points, we can use nc3 to outline a triangle, and multiply 3 for the 3 options of sides we could remove to make two edges intersecting at one point. if there are 4 points, we note that given any 4 points, just using those configurations, there are only 3 possible ways to make edges with all points. Therefore, we can say that (nc2)c2=3(nc3)+3(nc4).\n</p><p>then go as above\n</p><p>~mrcosmic\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II\" title=\"2022 AIME II\">2022 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2022\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2022 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018020545\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.072 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 478/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1808/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 130/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16983/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.874      1 -total\n 57.53%    7.981      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.97%    5.546      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21814:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018020545 and revision id 291017. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}